entry.summary:
Cypress is one of the most popular E2E testing frameworks for web applications. But testing email flows in Cypress has always required either a running mail server or mocking the email layer entirely. This guide shows how to test real email flows in Cypress — verification emails, OTP codes, magic links, and password resets — without Docker, without MailHog, and without mocking. Most Cypress setups for email testing fall into one of three categories: 1. Mock the email service cy.intercept('POST', '/api/send-email', { statusCode: 200 });
Fast, but tests nothing. If your email template has a broken link, this passes. 2. Use MailHog services: mailhog: image: mailhog/mailhog ports: - 1025:1025 - 8025:8025
Requires Docker in CI, 15-30 seconds cold start, shared inbox brea…
